  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "First Bohr orbit of $\\mathrm{H}$ atom has radius\n$$\n\\mathrm{r}=0.529 Å\n$$\nAlso, the angular momentum is quantised.\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\mathrm{mvr}=\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{2 \\pi} \\\\\n&2 \\pi \\mathrm{r}=\\frac{\\mathrm{h}}{\\mathrm{mv}}=\\lambda \\\\\n&\\lambda=2 \\pi \\times 0.529 Å\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
